{
  "description": "captured-admission.v0 conformance vectors — the shared lifecycle CORE under review verdicts, contribution settlement, and TEE attestation epochs. Every verdict recomputed by admission_check.py from the record + an explicit as_of alone. Two stored dimensions (lifecycle_state, disposition) in separate namespaces; absence (liveness_failure) and conflict are DERIVED. Admission is a GATE (only accepted creates an obligation). Semantic resolution and liveness are separate facts; a late disposition resolves without erasing the breach. Five control families shaped by Pavlo's PR #5 blind-diff: as_of gates (future events ignored on an earlier snapshot), open vocabulary (unrecognized kind != rejected:<echo>), enumerability (sequence completeness/continuity), capture provenance (core binding/signature/anchor/timing + profile-owned role/anchor-class), authority transitions (expiry/ordering/rollback/conflict).",
